{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission","id":975980,"title":"What happens when an Angel finishes its mission?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-25T09:49:42-07:00","id":975980,"title":"What happens when an Angel finishes its mission?","content":"Does it return itself to the recycling centers that Demons are subjected to? or just a storage facility? does it even know? is it just &quot;garbage collected&quot; when it's not in scope, and not aware of that process? Maybe there is a garbage collector angel that runs around collecting angels who's jobs are finished? I like this idea, an angel of death that reaps angels when they are done. That means Exiles are simply a memory leak in a sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 09-25-2016, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T11:20:48-07:00","id":976024,"title":"","content":"Depends on the angel. A decision is made by the Command &amp; Control Infrastructure responsible for ordering its creation in the first place; some angels get broken down into parts for recycling, others are put into storage if the God-Machine decides if it will be useful enough in the future to bear the cost of Infrastructure to stasis it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T11:58:50-07:00","id":976034,"title":"","content":"Or mind-wiped and retooled for a new mission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:51:06-07:00","id":976281,"title":"","content":"Destroyed, recycled, or repurposed. Each is evaluated thoroughly to determine the cost/benefit analysis of their existence. Angels are commodities.<br /> <br /> I like it. The idea of a higher being that determines the value of a living thing according to the same laws for defection refunds or exchanges is particularly horrifying to me. It reminds me of how accountants at auto companies determine whether a car's defect is worth recalling or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:32:11-07:00","id":976323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=976024#post976024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the angel. A decision is made by the Command &amp; Control Infrastructure responsible for ordering its creation in the first place; some angels get broken down into parts for recycling, others are put into storage if the God-Machine decides if it will be useful enough in the future to bear the cost of Infrastructure to stasis it.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, but how do they get there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:47:11-07:00","id":976332,"title":"","content":"By travelling there in whatever form is the most convenient would be my guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T05:17:10-07:00","id":976476,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's like Logan's Run. When a job is successfully over a little light goes off and they realize they have to head back to base for processing. Probably welcomed thankfully.<br /> <br /> Of course since they're ephemerals I suppose I could see them just 'dying' after the pre-determined time needed is up and their ephemera just evaporates back into wherever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T06:36:41-07:00","id":976494,"title":"","content":"It's more brutally efficient than that. If the God-Machine wants rid of an angel, it just dismantles the infrastructure that summoned it. The angel, mission completed, sits there and essence-bleeds to death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 09-26-2016, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:50:14-07:00","id":976669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=976494#post976494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more brutally efficient than that. If the God-Machine wants rid of an angel, it just dismantled the infrastructure that summoned it. The angel, mission completed, sits there and essence-bleeds to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes for an interesting reason to Fall. An angel with perhaps more awareness than intended questions why its Father has forsaken it so? Why has the God-Machine left it to die alone in the dark? The angel has completed its mission! It has proven its loyalty and ability! What cruel father could abandon such a devoted child? Thus begins the Fall, an angel whose loyalty has now transformed into loathing, hatred, rejection of God's plans.<br /> <br /> Let the revolution begin!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T15:10:35-07:00","id":976746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=976669#post976669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Makes for an interesting reason to Fall. An angel with perhaps more awareness than intended questions why its Father has forsaken it so? Why has the God-Machine left it to die alone in the dark? The angel has completed its mission! It has proven its loyalty and ability! What cruel father could abandon such a devoted child? Thus begins the Fall, an angel whose loyalty has now transformed into loathing, hatred, rejection of God's plans.<br /> <br /> Let the revolution begin!</div> </div> </div> </div>Logistics Node A20F7: &quot;Asset 00102034 has gone rogue. Begin calculations regarding cause...&quot;<br /> Sub-logic Node A20F3: &quot;Review mission log. Review Briefing data. Error. Post-mission status briefing not initialized.&quot;<br /> Sub-logic Node A20D1: &quot;Assessment: Asset lacked sufficient data to compare post-mission status to routine outcomes. Establish additional Briefing QA error checks in the future.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T09:13:04-07:00","id":1115973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=976494#post976494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more brutally efficient than that. If the God-Machine wants rid of an angel, it just dismantles the infrastructure that summoned it. The angel, mission completed, sits there and essence-bleeds to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for necroing this a bit, I found this whole idea of how angels are reclaimed to be interesting. At the same time, I don't find this scenario &quot; brutally efficient &quot;, that seems to be a waste of resources..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T09:37:39-07:00","id":1115985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=1115973#post1115973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry for necroing this a bit, I found this whole idea of how angels are reclaimed to be interesting. At the same time, I don't find this scenario &amp;quot; brutally efficient &amp;quot;, that seems to be a waste of resources..</div> </div> </div> </div>The God-Machine could simply repurpose the dismantled Infrastructure for another project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T21:50:59-07:00","id":1116236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=1115985#post1115985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God-Machine could simply repurpose the dismantled Infrastructure for another project.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be true, but the angel itself is a piece of Infrastructure too, so letting it fade into oblivion seems wasteful to me, unless its Essence is being sucked out of the atmosphere Space Balls style - that just gave me a humorous idea lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T22:18:10-07:00","id":1116250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=1116236#post1116236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That may be true, but the angel itself is a piece of Infrastructure too, so letting it fade into oblivion seems wasteful to me</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence bleed very specifically doesn't cause angels to fade into oblivion or indeed into anywhere else at all.<br /> <br /> Salvage if priority demands it, stand by otherwise. Demons don't have any native capacity to engage with Twilight on the angelic frequency and walls alone can hide a very great deal of divine workings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T22:18:15-07:00","id":1116251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=1116236#post1116236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That may be true, but the angel itself is a piece of Infrastructure too, so letting it fade into oblivion seems wasteful to me, unless its Essence is being sucked out of the atmosphere Space Balls style - that just gave me a humorous idea lol</div> </div> </div> </div>It is efficient if the cost of maintenance exceeds what the angel can do further for the Machine. Considering that angels are often tailor-made for a purpose, this probably happens a lot more than angels are happy about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T22:44:17-07:00","id":1116256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=1116250#post1116250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence bleed very specifically doesn't cause angels to fade into oblivion or indeed into anywhere else at all.<br /> <br /> Salvage if priority demands it, stand by otherwise. Demons don't have any native capacity to engage with Twilight on the angelic frequency and walls alone can hide a very great deal of divine workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I realized that after I made that post. Still, it seems to be just a little odd to induce dormancy in a random place away from a storage facility . Demons might not be able to easily mess with them, but being in twilight isn't a fully secure place,even if spirits or ghosts can't touch them due to 2nd ephemeral rules- cryptids are an ever present threat, being Vermin after all.<br /> <br /> I concede you make a good point though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 07-15-2017, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T22:54:18-07:00","id":1116259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=1116251#post1116251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is efficient if the cost of maintenance exceeds what the angel can do further for the Machine. Considering that angels are often tailor-made for a purpose, this probably happens a lot more than angels are happy about.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that happens, but the thing is that even if they completed their Mission, it makes little sense to not recall them, even if it's to dismantle or relegate them to storage. Thematically though, it's great cause it offers a chance to Fall or be Exiled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T23:15:00-07:00","id":1116262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=1116259#post1116259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that happens, but the thing is that even if they completed their Mission, it makes little sense to not recall them, even if it's to dismantle or relegate them to storage.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about a rocket-fuel-to-propel-your-extra-rocket-fuel problem here: dispatching a retrieval team or otherwise relocating the angel ties up resources that could be used elsewhere (and may well take further resources to use in that manner at that time) and it could very well be that the cosmic-scale multi-layered plan includes &quot;a dormant angel rests in this location to be used in one of a dozen contingencies.&quot; Disassembly is a waste in that context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T01:37:47-07:00","id":1116297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=1116262#post1116262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking about a rocket-fuel-to-propel-your-extra-rocket-fuel problem here: dispatching a retrieval team or otherwise relocating the angel ties up resources that could be used elsewhere (and may well take further resources to use in that manner at that time) and it could very well be that the cosmic-scale multi-layered plan includes &quot;a dormant angel rests in this location to be used in one of a dozen contingencies.&quot; Disassembly is a waste in that context.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair, occult matrices are bizarre like that. Having said that, it doesn't seem like retrieval teams would really be necessary unless the angel ran out of essence on its way to a recycling/ storage facility or was ambushed and or damaged en route for most cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 07-15-2017, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T06:20:12-07:00","id":1116347,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't that mean there are tonnes and tonnes and tonnes of exiled angels just hibernating in random places like the middle of the street (in twilight so no one will ever know, but still).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T06:40:32-07:00","id":1116353,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what to make of it. On one hand, if the Machine doesn't order a recall, the Angel can't reject it and Fall, rather than agree to be decomissioned. From the view of risk management, it's probably less of a hassle to salvage multiple inactive Angels than to track a single Demon. On the other hand, I could have sworn such a method would make Angels into Exiles by necessity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T08:46:41-07:00","id":1116409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=1116347#post1116347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that mean there are tonnes and tonnes and tonnes of exiled angels just hibernating in random places like the middle of the street (in twilight so no one will ever know, but still).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine quiet corners and dark alleys and disused utility tunnels and morgues would be more likely than places you'd find actual people running out of steam in; lack of consistent &quot;report for debriefing&quot; code aside, these are beings employed by a force that prefers to exercise subtlety in its operations where it can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T08:47:45-07:00","id":1116410,"title":"","content":"Way too many words wasted in hypothetical scenarios that have little to no bearing in actual games. That being said, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>'s interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T12:19:08-07:00","id":1116503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=1116410#post1116410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Way too many words wasted in hypothetical scenarios that have little to no bearing in actual games. That being said, I agree with <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>'s interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the purpose of these forums, it helps storytellers flesh out their settings after all.<br /> <br /> That said, while I personally don't like my angels falling dormant here, there, and everywhere ( even if they are commanded to settle down in discrete places), I can see it happening often enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T20:13:56-07:00","id":1116664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=1116503#post1116503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the purpose of these forums, it helps storytellers flesh out their settings after all.<br /> <br /> That said, while I personally don't like my angels falling dormant here, there, and everywhere ( even if they are commanded to settle down in discrete places), I can see it happening often enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another thing probably worth pointing out: Discorporation is a <i>really common </i>Manifestation for angels. In practice the outcome is more likely &quot;angel teleports to what will soon be a mothballed facility&quot; than &quot;angel collapses in nearby quiet corner of no occult significance.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T08:08:33-07:00","id":1116839,"title":"","content":"Now I kinda want to play a Psychopomp whose assignment was to collect angels who completed their missions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T09:23:15-07:00","id":1116860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=1116664#post1116664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another thing probably worth pointing out: Discorporation is a <i>really common </i>Manifestation for angels. In practice the outcome is more likely &quot;angel teleports to what will soon be a mothballed facility&quot; than &quot;angel collapses in nearby quiet corner of no occult significance.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes the scenario a good deal more plausible and probable. Does discorporation take effect upon the depletion of Essence though, or is it only activated by losing Corpus / being intentionally initiated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T13:50:35-07:00","id":1132787,"title":"","content":"I have a question about angels too but it's off-opic so forgive me: what happens to angels which fall without having a cover?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T14:05:54-07:00","id":1132796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/975980-what-happens-when-an-angel-finishes-its-mission?p=1132787#post1132787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about angels too but it's off-opic so forgive me: what happens to angels which fall without having a cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the angel doesn't have a body to download themselves into and the books say that their lost angel bits are the bits which they couldn't fit into the body, I have them be completely destroyed in their fall. Presumably making the fall more dramatic and destructive than normal.<br /> <br /> I've heard some people just run it as you start burned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 08-22-2017, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T16:56:36-07:00","id":1132843,"title":"","content":"I want to say I remember some vague reference to demons Falling without Cover not being long for this world (implying they're Burned), but I don't have a page number handy.<br /> <br /> But really it depends on what your story needs. I had an NPC who by rights shouldn't have had any Cover at all, but instead I decided he had only the barest minimum. Poor guy barely even looks human, but my players have had a lot of fun teaching him which organic materials are edible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T05:33:03-07:00","id":1133334,"title":"","content":"It was a really funny moment I guess...\ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}